{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost","id":175983,"title":"Werewolf's \"ghost\"?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-21T07:48:20-07:00","id":175983,"title":"Werewolf's \"ghost\"?","content":"So I have idea for my Sweden chronicle that players will hear a legend of old pre-Viking era werewolf &quot;chief&quot; who &quot;was blessed by gods and collected powerful weapons&quot; ( i.e. many klaives <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). So I will lead my players to look for the lost tomb of &quot;hero&quot; for it's treasures. As with this kind of &quot;ghost stories&quot;, I would want the original owner return to them as ghost they will need to fight of in final of the story. But I'm also remembering there was in gameline something about Uratha not leaving ghosts, but ancestral spirits? So can werewolf have ghost, and if not, how the ancestral spirits different from it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T08:18:56-07:00","id":176010,"title":"","content":"Couple of misconceptions: Ancestor spirits aren't a single Uratha's representation, but the spiritual representation of a whole bloodline of Uratha. Many may take the most recognizable traits of the most renowned, famous and celebrated Uratha of said bloodline, but you should keep in mind that the spirit isn't singular, it's plural.<br /> <br /> Indeed, werewolves are assumed not to leave shades after they die... But what if this particular one did? Why? How? Was he cursed? How can he be put to rest? Alternatively, can't you use an Ancestor spirit there instead of a ghost? The same feel can be easily achieved with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T08:34:56-07:00","id":176018,"title":"","content":"Canonicaly, i think that werewolfs cannot become ghosts but werewolfs with a enough high Primal Urge can become spirits after death. <br /> But you can makes otherly if you want but that removes a potentially interesting theme (Werewolves have souls or they are spirits in flesh, no realy more than the Urged/Claimed ?).<br /> <br /> Maybe y you can create a threat of ghosts werewolves and insisting that this is supposed to be<i> impossible. </i>(which can make it more disturbing : &quot;simples&quot; ghosts don't seems necessarily for werewolves who deals with spirits; but impossible ghosts ? it adds mystery)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T08:49:04-07:00","id":176040,"title":"","content":"This particular &quot;ghost&quot; is after a true bloody werewolf warlord that made a slaughter of local werebears in his living. He still thinks he made just thing, but bear spirits cursed him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=176010#post176010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couple of misconceptions: Ancestor spirits aren't a single Uratha's representation, but the spiritual representation of a whole bloodline of Uratha. Many may take the most recognizable traits of the most renowned, famous and celebrated Uratha of said bloodline, but you should keep in mind that the spirit isn't singular, it's plural.<br /> <br /> Indeed, werewolves are assumed not to leave shades after they die... But what if this particular one did? Why? How? Was he cursed? How can he be put to rest? Alternatively, can't you use an Ancestor spirit there instead of a ghost? The same feel can be easily achieved with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this is out of question, because I was thinking about this particular individual werewolf. Really, I'm looking on something as most as human &quot;ghost&quot; an Uratha can have. If nothing other comes up as better solution I will make him ancestral spirit, but he would be &quot;ghost in the disguise&quot; then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=176018#post176018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Canonicaly, i think that werewolfs cannot become ghosts but werewolfs with a enough high Primal Urge can become spirits after death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other spirits than Ancestors? Like not &quot;Spirit of Bloody Vikings&quot;, but &quot;Spirit of Rognvald, the Bear Killer&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=176018#post176018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe y you can create a threat of ghosts werewolves and insisting that this is supposed to be<i> impossible. </i>(which can make it more disturbing : &quot;simples&quot; ghosts don't seems necessarily for werewolves who deals with spirits; but impossible ghosts ? it adds mystery)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still buffered you can summon the &quot;Spirit&quot; ( truly ghost ) of your named ancestors. Why can't young werewolf summon his centrues great hero forfather when werewolves are half spiritual beings? Werewolf can summon his whole bloodline spirit, but not his great-grandfather that was Uratha legend? Why is this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T08:54:22-07:00","id":176042,"title":"","content":"Well perhaps, a ghost werewolf leaves a wolf geist behind. O.o","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T08:59:57-07:00","id":176044,"title":"","content":"Well, this gets into the metaphysics of the World of Darkness ephemeral entities a bit. Everything in the world of darkness, except humans, have spiritual reflections (not necessarily every individual thing, but there are spirits of everything). Likewise, humans seem to be the only things that leave ghosts after they die. So there seems to be a certain amount of mutual exclusivity, and since werewolves are part spirit, it makes sense they would not be able to create ghosts. Although on the other hand, they are part human. You could always say that in your particular take on the setting, a Werewolf's spirit side lives on after the death of their physical body, unless what ever killed them destroyed the spirit as well as the flesh - a supernatural attack, or silver might do that, but a wood chipper might not. That would give them a human-like tendency to leave echoes, without that echo being the ghost of a wolf or a spirit. Also consider that, especially with the new ephemeral entity rules, the only real mechanical difference between ghosts and spirits is their influences and starting manifestation condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T10:28:51-07:00","id":176113,"title":"","content":"Ancestor-spirits are not ghosts or the souls of dead people returning to the world of the living. An ancestor-spirit is a spiritual amalgamation of an entire bloodline, the wisdom and personalities of generations given a single spiritual form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T10:28:58-07:00","id":176114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=176044#post176044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could always say that in your particular take on the setting, a Werewolf's spirit side lives on after the death of their physical body, unless what ever killed them destroyed the spirit as well as the flesh - a supernatural attack, or silver might do that, but a wood chipper might not. That would give them a human-like tendency to leave echoes, without that echo being the ghost of a wolf or a spirit. Also consider that, especially with the new ephemeral entity rules, the only real mechanical difference between ghosts and spirits is their influences and starting manifestation condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more inclined to treat &quot;ghost&quot; werewolves as minor spirits. You can summon your great-grandfather, and he won't be merely shade of himself. He would be quasi-material spirit of his great deeds and legend. To be frank, he would be story of your grandfathers deeds, than less his own memories. And I would treat them as half ghost, half spirits. They are just Ancestors. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-21-2014, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T11:15:15-07:00","id":176223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=176113#post176113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ancestor-spirits are not ghosts or the souls of dead people returning to the world of the living. An ancestor-spirit is a spiritual amalgamation of an entire bloodline, the wisdom and personalities of generations given a single spiritual form.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So after death, even if corebook says you become a spirit, you are not? Possibly joining only Ancestor Spirit of the bloodline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T11:55:02-07:00","id":176254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=176113#post176113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ancestor-spirits are not ghosts or the souls of dead people returning to the world of the living. An ancestor-spirit is a spiritual amalgamation of an entire bloodline, the wisdom and personalities of generations given a single spiritual form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got any Backing on that one? Sounds like opinion to me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T12:02:06-07:00","id":176257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=176254#post176254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got any Backing on that one? Sounds like opinion to me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Lodges the Faithful, Page 38, under 'Ancestor-Spirits.' It's the first lines, word for word.<br /> <br /> Here's the rest:<br /> Therefore, Cerberans are not oath-bound to destroy ancestor-spirits and prevent them from ever in\ufb02uencing the living. However, in reality, this is for any individual Uratha to decide where her beliefs fall on the matter. Few Lodge of Cerberus werewolves hate or dislike ancestor-spirits, but few would ever bond themselves to one as a pack totem either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=176223#post176223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So after death, even if corebook says you become a spirit, you are not? Possibly joining only Ancestor Spirit of the bloodline?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe the corebook says that werewolves become spirits after death. It's possible for them to become one with an ancestral spirit, but otherwise when a werewolf dies they just die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-21-2014, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T12:09:15-07:00","id":176263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=176254#post176254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Got any Backing on that one? Sounds like opinion to me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Lore of the Forsaken, pg19; Predators pg64.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T13:48:18-07:00","id":176381,"title":"","content":"I thought more on matter, and as I understand the gameline idea of Ancestor-spirits, it's not exactly what I would want to have in my games. To be precises, I want them and quasi-ghost werewolf spirits that are probably proto-Ancestor-spirits like developers envision them. So here is my take on the subject. I thought more on matter, and as I understand the gameline idea of Ancestor-spirits, it's not exactly what I would want to have in my games. To be precises, I want them and quasi-ghost werewolf spirits that are probably proto-Ancestor-spirits like developers envision them. So here is my take on the subject.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Ancestor ( ephemeral being )</b></i><br /> Uratha are cretures of both flesh and spirit. Legend say's that sometime one of powerful werewolves is rewarded by spirits for his duty by lingering after his death as concept of his dedication. Those ephemeral beings are called Ancestors.<br /> <br /> Ancestors are entities on verge of two worlds. They are mostly a spirits, but they are based on individual werewolves personality, like ghosts are for humans. But, in reality, are spirits of duties and deeds particular Uratha embodied in his life, not echeos of his own psyche. Those that knows the Geists of Underworld say that Ancestors are \u201csecond part of the puzzle\u201d - if Geists are ghost that by become some part spirits, Ancestors are spirits that are based on vague after image of werewolves soul that would become ghost \u2013 if werewolves weren't half spirits themselves. Ancestor is this spiritual part of one of People that linger after his death in Shadow Realm, bounded by eternal duties he himself made in his life.<br /> <br /> But this honor is reserved only for most dedicated and spiritual of Uratha. Sometime Ancestors of one bloodline merge in one more powerful being that is more representation of families history as a whole. With each merging of Ancestors, family spirits are less and less about individual members duty and memory, but more about linage of bloodline as a whole. Most of the time individual Ancestors can linger as themselves only few centuries in Shadow Realm before merging with families spirits, but this period varies on each case. Some cheat this system by bounding with fetishes or places, like they own tombs, laying dormant for years, starving for Essence.<br /> <br /> <i><b>System</b></i><br /> <b>Notice:</b> Rules below assume usage of <b>God Machine Chronicles</b> ephemeral rules and cosmology so if you didn't readed before \u2013 get the PDF for free and compare to those mechanics. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Ancestors are new type of spirits that are created after very powerful werewolf dies. To become one, Uratha need to have Primal Urge 6 or more and he become Ancestor Spirits of Rank equal to his Primal Urge \u2013 5. His Attributes are average of all three in his corporal categories, just like ghosts are. His Renown becomes his Influences as Ancestor, even if they are higher than his normal Rank. His Gifts become Numina, but only those that he can use in his new, ephemeral state. Bans and Banes varies, but Ancestors mostly cultivate their restrictions from Tribe, Lodge or Totem patrons.<br /> <i><b>Example:</b></i><br /> <i>Rongvald Paws Crusher is powerful Uratha that is slain on his line of duty. Spirits are rewarding him with joining as one of them, so he becomes Ancestor. He has Primal Urge 7 and Renowns of Purity 4, Cunning 3 and Glory 2. He becomes Rank 2 spirit with Purity 4, Cunning 3 and Glory 2 as it's Influances, even the both Purity and Cunning are higher than his Rank.</i><br /> <br /> Family spirits are beings called in <b>Lore of Forasken</b> and <b>Predators</b> as Ancestors-spirits.<br /> <br /> So what do you think on this setting shard?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T14:33:48-07:00","id":176429,"title":"","content":"Point of order: the definite bit of metaphysics is not &quot;werewolves don't leave ghosts.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's &quot;werewolf ghosts do not descend to the Underworld.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T22:25:52-07:00","id":177684,"title":"","content":"There's another take you might consider.<br /> <br /> Werewolves age half as fast as normal people, and it's believed that increasing primal urge slows that down even further.<br /> <br /> So elder werewolves spend more and more time in the hisil and become more and more spirit like.<br /> <br /> So, what if your &quot;werewolf ghost&quot; is an elder werewolf who became a full spirit instead of dying?<br /> <br /> In second sight one storyline was about a spell that turned an occultist into a spirit. If a spiritually null human can achieve it, a werewolf, who is halfway there to begin with, certainly ought to be able to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T22:49:54-07:00","id":177698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=177684#post177684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's another take you might consider.<br /> <br /> Werewolves age half as fast as normal people, and it's believed that increasing primal urge slows that down even further.<br /> <br /> So elder werewolves spend more and more time in the hisil and become more and more spirit like.<br /> <br /> So, what if your &quot;werewolf ghost&quot; is an elder werewolf who became a full spirit instead of dying?<br /> <br /> In second sight one storyline was about a spell that turned an occultist into a spirit. If a spiritually null human can achieve it, a werewolf, who is halfway there to begin with, certainly ought to be able to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>See also: ancestor spirits and the seeming in-universe confusion between the Firstborn and the First Pack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T03:49:48-07:00","id":177813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=176044#post176044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise, humans seem to be the only things that leave ghosts after they die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not true. Buildings, animals, even geographic features can leave ghosts behind when destroyed or killed. Ghosts are semi-psychic in nature - if enough people <i>remember</i> something, and its loss was especially traumatic, it makes a Ghost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T05:42:05-07:00","id":177859,"title":"","content":"Not to be argumentative, but according to pg. 215 of the GMC Ghosts are defined as dead humans. Ghostly reflections of places and things exist in the Underworld (as per Book of the Dead, and following your guidelines), but that wouldn't be the same thing as a Ghost, not in the context being discussed here. Unless it's changed in IC, dead Werewolves don't create Ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T07:35:53-07:00","id":177906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=176263#post176263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lore of the Forsaken, pg19; Predators pg64.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank You. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Not that I thought that Ancestor Spirits were Ghosts (I don't), but I was looking for clarification on your second point (the amalgamation of an Entire Line).<br /> I will peruse the references provided. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T09:59:33-07:00","id":178039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=177906#post177906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank You. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Not that I thought that Ancestor Spirits were Ghosts (I don't), but I was looking for clarification on your second point (the amalgamation of an Entire Line).<br /> I will peruse the references provided. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/LSVMhOk.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T12:53:19-07:00","id":178144,"title":"","content":"Just was not something I remembered reading, and wanted sources so I could look them up. There is no need for malicious intent for sources to be inaccurate. Happens all the time. The Internet is a vast place, and not all sources are created equally. No offense was intended. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T02:39:23-07:00","id":181785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=177859#post177859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to be argumentative, but according to pg. 215 of the GMC Ghosts are defined as dead humans. Ghostly reflections of places and things exist in the Underworld (as per Book of the Dead, and following your guidelines), but that wouldn't be the same thing as a Ghost, not in the context being discussed here. Unless it's changed in IC, dead Werewolves don't create Ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div> Be that as it may, but some books contradict that.<br /> <br /> There's a literal ghost town in one book, complete with numina, and it exists in twilight.<br /> <br /> There's another story that has a ghost road, a dead end. <br /> <br /> Second Sight suggests that if the ST wants, spirits can become ghosts, and ghosts might become spirits.<br /> <br /> \u200b And if we're using &quot;ghosts have to be human first so werewolves need not apply&quot; than the vampire ghost in night horrors and the ghost mages in the mage core book are a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T03:50:00-07:00","id":181812,"title":"","content":"Yep, there are ghosts that weren't human before. Objects can leave ghosts behind as can places. Some are even somewhat sentient. Ghost mages are definetly a thing (but among all the supernatural creatures are arguably the most human), vampire ghosts appear here and there in some official books, and the concept is too cool not to use it. Werewolves being half-spirit, and spirit-ghost being most of the time mutually exclusive states (except for Geist hybrids) makes it more complicated, but they are also part human, so why not? In the worst case they become some sort of wolf geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T05:44:24-07:00","id":181844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=181812#post181812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the worst case they become some sort of wolf geist.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's exaclty what I was proposing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T16:12:05-08:00","id":1053488,"title":"","content":"In my take on the CofD, I like to imply that the forsaken tribes sometimes have their own afterlives beliefs in the vein of the Fired Touched one, and in fact may have started the stories in response to the fire touched.<br /> <br /> If they exist, they are the personal Shadow Kingdoms of the Forsaken First Born, which I make by mashing together the appropriate WtA umbra realms. Red Wolf's domain/ The Iron Master afterlife (I like to call it &quot;The City&quot; but in first tongue), for example, is sort of a mash up of the more high tech umbra realms, with the Glass Walker and Bone Gnawer homelands turning into the &quot;residential&quot; sections of the Iron Master afterlife and the Cyber Realm and Scar becoming the commercial and industrial sectors/&quot;hunting ground&quot; (the more dangerous humans are literally there to be hunted, any Iron master that gets &quot;killed&quot; on one these eternal hunts just wakes up in their apartment or penthouse in the home and instead of Wyrm and Weaver Spirits running things as the Barons of industry such, it's red wolf and his council of his 2nd born wolf spirit children and the greatest heroes of the Iron Masters.<br /> <br /> And when I said the humans in the not-Scar and not-cyber-realm exist to be hunted, I mean that humans killed in an Iron Master Sacred Hunt wind up in those areas of Red Wolf's domain, to be hunted and killed again and again for all eternity. Human and wolf-blooded packmates of Iron Masters, on the other hand, wind up &quot;living&quot; with their Uratha packmates in the residential areas.<br /> <br /> The other forsaken tribes have something similar going on.<br /> <br /> I am trying to come with cool names for the neighborhoods that sound cool in first tongue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T17:00:56-08:00","id":1053514,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3932_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3932\" data-vbnamecard=\"3932\">The young man in the cafe</a> Well, considering Firstborns are rank 7 and basically near infinite essence, and 5 dots in influence is &quot;Mass Create&quot; they indeed can have huge &quot;places-that-aren't&quot; realms hidden deeply in the Shadow. Hell, some legends even hint at those, and how the would be Forsaken had to get there to truck with their would be eventual totems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T21:19:57-08:00","id":1053619,"title":"","content":"I'm under the impression that ghosts are more of an emotional resonance so intense that it takes on a form of its own, reenacting that emotion (and the trauma that created it) over and over with varying degrees of sophistication.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor this story I would skip the whole question of werewolf ghosts and do they have an afterlife (personally I figure either the Anima Mundi, or wherever in the deep shadow spirits go when forced to discorporate). Instead I would create something symbolic, similar to a ghost's anchor, say a throne made from the skulls of the were-bears he killed with his corpse still seated upon it (trapped in Gauru representing the unnatural nature of the werewolf's trapped spirit) and then have the werewolf (just as written on his character sheet) trapped in Twilight, unable to enter the Hisil or manifest away from his throne. Instead he is dependent upon his gifts and his own form of Sacred Hunt (which makes him all too real to his prey) to effect the material world.<br /> In the end to defeat him the players have to kick over his throne, spilling his mummified corpse onto the ground where it returns to human form and his spirit goes screaming (or gratefully) to wherever werewolf spirits go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T16:06:40-08:00","id":1054066,"title":"","content":"My fanon:<br /> High Harmony werewolves leave ghosts, but in the Hisil. Such ghosts may become stranger things over time.<br /> Low Harmony werewolves become spirits.<br /> Harmony 5 is the werewolf equivalent of Integrity 10 for a human, leaving nothing behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T07:02:01-08:00","id":1054295,"title":"","content":"It's also possible that a powerful-enough werewolf, perhaps slain while attempting a Sacred Hunt, could leave a ghost <i>and</i> a spirit. That's certainly the idea that I'm going to run with in my Forsaken game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T08:37:51-08:00","id":1054332,"title":"","content":"If a werewolf could leave a ghost or a spirit under the same circumstances (if there's an overlap in Harmony requirements, for example) it'd actually be weird if they wouldn't be able to leave both at the same time. Ghosts are not direct continuations of people. Ghosts don't even necessarily require people to die. While undoubtedly rare a ghost could spring into existence from a near-death experience.<br /> But then there's also all the weird stuff that just happens. Occurrences that just don't follow the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T09:51:04-08:00","id":1054353,"title":"","content":"If a werewolf would leave a spirit when they die, they'd likely have left a spirit before they die. Spirits are reflections of reality, if the werewolf is somehow powerful enough to make a reflection, it would be spawning spirits before its death. In fact, when it did die unless it was tied to something else like a worshiping pack or lodge, there's no reason to think they would leave a spirit behind when they died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T16:26:19-08:00","id":1054498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=1054353#post1054353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits are reflections of reality, if the werewolf is somehow powerful enough to make a reflection, it would be spawning spirits before its death.</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes you think it's spirit of the hunt half isn't consuming all the essence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T17:56:31-08:00","id":1054538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=1054498#post1054498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes you think it's spirit of the hunt half isn't consuming all the essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Essence Cap, lack of being in the Hisil 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, etc, the fact that you don't get your Essence back when you use Gifts and other abilities, totems existing and flourishing from the activities of werewolves, the many other spirits that follow werewolves around to feed on the Essence borne of their activities and the spirits that are borne of the acts of werewolves, the need for the Sacred Hunt rite.<br /> <br /> Basically everything in the setting.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you can't have a spirit that comes after your death, except for the lack of 'person' spirits, but there's far more spirits coming from your actions before your death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-24-2017, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T18:13:28-08:00","id":1054555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=1054538#post1054538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Essence Cap, lack of being in the Hisil 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, etc,</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to be in Hisil... Essence is created in the mortal world and then eventually filters into the Hisil through the gauntlet. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the fact that you don't get your Essence back when you use Gifts and other abilities, totems existing and flourishing from the activities of werewolves, the many other spirits that follow werewolves around to feed on the Essence borne of their activities and the spirits that are borne of the acts of werewolves, the need for the Sacred Hunt rite.<br /> <br /> Basically everything in the setting.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you can't have a spirit that comes after your death, except for the lack of 'person' spirits, but there's far more spirits coming from your actions before your death. </div> </div> </div>I think you have misunderstood what I meant by all. I'm meaning all the &quot;you&quot; essence which would lead to there being a &quot;you spirit&quot;, not &quot;eats every bit of resonance which comes as a result of your actions&quot;. I mean there's a reason why you need to do the sacred hunt regularly, your spirit self needs that resonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T18:34:47-08:00","id":1054563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=1054555#post1054555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need to be in Hisil... Essence is created in the mortal world and then eventually filters into the Hisil through the gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>You would need to be in the Hisil for your spirit side to eat said Essence, like all the other spirits that eat the Essence created by werewolves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you have misunderstood what I meant by all. I'm meaning all the &quot;you&quot; essence which would lead to there being a &quot;you spirit&quot;, not &quot;eats every bit of resonance which comes as a result of your actions&quot;. I mean there's a reason why you need to do the sacred hunt regularly, your spirit self needs that resonance. </div> </div> </div>This seems like the kind of thing that would be explained in a sidebar in the Empty Wolves section, as they have had their souls removed and consequently the part of the spirit of the hunt.<br /> <br /> For whatever reason, there isn't any 'you' spirits for anyone, werewolf or no. The only exception seems to be the twin spirits from a Wolf-Blooded Tell, which aren't really a spirit of 'you' anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T01:31:32-08:00","id":1054681,"title":"","content":"I always thought that Uratha upon death become spirits of their own Renowns, something like wolves Lunes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T15:39:04-08:00","id":1054965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=1054563#post1054563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You would need to be in the Hisil for your spirit side to eat said Essence, like all the other spirits that eat the Essence created by werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes you think that? No spirit needs to be in hisil to consume essence. Better access to edible essence is the whole point of spirits leaving the hisil.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This seems like the kind of thing that would be explained in a sidebar in the Empty Wolves section, as they have had their souls removed and consequently the part of the spirit of the hunt. </div> </div> </div>Not really, since they don't t<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For whatever reason, there isn't any 'you' spirits for anyone, werewolf or no. The only exception seems to be the twin spirits from a Wolf-Blooded Tell, which aren't really a spirit of 'you' anyways. </div> </div> </div>Except there is for werewolves after they die. Ancestor spirits and a type of immundi. And you said &quot;If a werewolf would leave a spirit when they die, they'd likely have left a spirit before they die.&quot; so I'm saying why those things don't conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T16:01:41-08:00","id":1054976,"title":"","content":"If you really want a revenant or ghost werewolf, my preferred option is: So terrifyingly <i>\u200bangry</i>\u200b that he or she fought their way back from the Unutterable that lies on the other side of the Eternal Boundary, smashed the gates of death back open by prying the echoes of Death Wolf's whispers from that non-state, and is now back to let everyone know that they've only gotten even more enraged by spending a few days/years/millennia in the void. Bolt on ab-natural horrors to suit (void spirits, abyssals, ghosts, whatever) to either a disembodied rage-spirit of utterly monstrous power, or a half-dead corpse-Uratha whose blood is running hot again from all that sheer, bottled up pissed-offness.<br /> <br /> \u200bI wouldn't worry too much about how to wangle a werewolf leaving a ghost via the standard metaphysics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T18:03:34-08:00","id":1055016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=1054965#post1054965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except there is for werewolves after they die. Ancestor spirits and a type of immundi. And you said &quot;If a werewolf would leave a spirit when they die, they'd likely have left a spirit before they die.&quot; so I'm saying why those things don't conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ancestor spirits are not a type of Immundi. Immundi are demon-tainted spirits, so rather than predate, they corrupt.<br /> <br /> Ancestor spirits are just a spirit of a focused family line, like the spirit of a political party or a football team. They don't even require a death to have occurred. The only reason one might be an Immundi is if it was tainted by a Wound or Whisperer. 'Ancestor-spirits are not ghosts or the souls of dead people returning to the world of the living. An ancestor-spirit is a spiritual amalgamation of an entire bloodline, the wisdom and personalities of generations given a single spiritual form.'<br /> <br /> There's no reason for a person, werewolf or no, to leave a spirit of themselves upon death. The how and why of their death is more likely to do so.<br /> <br /> And as usual I like Acrozatarim's idea. It's the difference between a ghost story with werewolves and a werewolf ghost story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-25-2017, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T19:21:36-08:00","id":1055038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=1055016#post1055016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ancestor spirits are not a type of Immundi. Immundi are demon-tainted spirits, so rather than predate, they corrupt.</div> </div> </div> </div>... I know. I said &quot;Ancestor spirits and a type of immundi&quot; not &quot;Ancestors spirits which are a type of immundi&quot;, since in addition to ancestor spirits being a sort of way to have dead werewolf spirits, there is a type of immundi which are meant to have been bale hounds who died.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T23:34:24-08:00","id":1055106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=1055038#post1055038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I know. I said &quot;Ancestor spirits and a type of immundi&quot; not &quot;Ancestors spirits which are a type of immundi&quot;, since in addition to ancestor spirits being a sort of way to have dead werewolf spirits, there is a type of immundi which are meant to have been bale hounds who died.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, it seemed like a typo.<br /> <br /> As you can see, ancestor spirits are 'not ghosts or the souls of dead people,' and the Maeladar you're referring to, if they exist, rely more on the power of the Maeljin than anything werewolves bring to the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-26-2017, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T11:06:02-08:00","id":1055713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1053245-do-werewolves-leave-ghosts-behind-when-they-die?p=1053312#post1053312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they do, it's never been mentioned. There's nothing explicitly saying they don't, but the one thing we can be sure of is werewolf ghosts, if they existed, wouldn't go to the Underworld.<br /> <br /> While they don't leave spirits behind, they traditionally have ancestor spirits. These are not really a spirit of an individual werewolf so much as the memories of a werewolfs lineage or family and legend.<br /> <br /> We've discussed it <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> As for devouring them for Essence, sure. It would justify a Breaking Point towards spirit, it's not a very fleshly thing to do.<br /> <br /> I don't believe you'd be able to learn Gifts from a Ghost, it's an inherently spirit-based phenomena, doing so would require a very unnatural ghost. But yes you could drain one of Essence to destroy it pretty easily, there's Lodges dedicated to it, such as the Lodge of Cerberus. A fetish that alters the Barghest Gift or some other fetish or Gift might do it as well.<br /> <br /> As for using the Sacred Hunt to do so, the rite does explicitly call for the Essence draining to be used on a spirit. But this is the kind of thing special lodge Sacred Hunt advantages can take care of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought this may be useful to the conversation.<br /> For your given chronicle I'd definitely rule that it was a Ghost, because that puts it outside of the purview of Spirit powers, and anchors to the very things the Players want to loot would be perfect way to keep the players involved.<br /> <br /> Remember Werewolves only see in the Spirit frequency of Twilight, not the Ghost, so it'd be a major blind spot that the ghost would be savvy enough to exploit.<br /> <br /> The Ghost could even be a Geist if it was the first being interned in the burial site, adding power to it. Imagine a Geist unable to enter the Underworld... That'd be scary.<br /> <br /> What your players will likely have to resort to deal with the strangeness caused by a Werewolf Chieftain Ghost:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF pg 140</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>SACRED HUNT (\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> The Sacred Hunt, the Siskur-Dah, is the most holy of all rites. Many werewolves believe that it draws upon the laws of the hunt that the Wolf-Mother herself personified.<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Symbols:</b> The hunt, prey, claws or weapons, blood Sample Rite: Blood Talon ritemasters commonly use a circling dance of participants, with the Urathas\u2019 claws marked with blood or ash. The ritemaster wears a mask representing the intended prey, and what follows is a mock-hunt around the dancing circle as the ritemaster seeks to break free. (Dexterity<br /> + Athletics)<br /> Action: Extended (10 successes; each roll represents 1<br /> minute)<br /> Success: The rite binds hunters and prey into the Siskur- Dah. All werewolves present are cast as the hunters. The ritemaster must indicate the intended prey during the rite, which can be an individual or a group, but they do not need to be identified with precise details or names.<br /> The rite has three effects:<br /> All participating werewolves gain the Siskur-Dah Condition.<br /> If the Uratha bring down a spirit that is the prey of this rite, they may divide its remaining Essence amongst themselves as they see fit; this can be used to destroy a spirit by draining all its Essence and discorporating it, but doing so is usually a breaking point toward Spirit and is seen as disrespectful if done without good reason.<br /> If the Uratha chase down spirit-prey that knows the symbols of a rite or can carve the secret of a Gift, any Uratha hunter present can expend the necessary Experiences to be marked with the Gift or learn the rite from the spirit. If this is done, the hunters do not get any Essence if they then bring the spirit down, and doing so is a breaking point toward Spirit.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF pg 310</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>SISKUR-DAH (PERSISTENT )</b><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Your character is on the Siskur-Dah, the Sacred Hunt. She gains a specific benefit depending on the ritemaster\u2019s tribe.<br /> <i>The Blood Talon </i>Sacred Hunt grants your character the ability to perceive the Renown brands of werewolf prey. She can see them as a clear silver glow (or a fiery red for Pure) and can read the prey\u2019s value in each Renown with a reflexive action.<br /> <i>The </i><i>Bone Shadow </i>Sacred Hunt grants your character the ability to touch and strike ephemeral entities nominated as prey with her natural weapons.<br /> <i>The Hunter in Darkness </i>Sacred Hunt grants your character the ability to sense the state of the Gauntlet in your presence; you are constantly aware of its current strength and if it has been increased or decreased compared to its normal strength; if the hunt\u2019s prey is responsible then you know this. You can also sense any other breaches in reality that your prey has moved through in the last lunar month \u2014 gateways to places and realms other than the Shadow.<br /> <i>The Iron Master </i>Sacred Hunt grants your character the ability to choose which of the Lunacy Conditions she inflicts on humans while hunting the prey.<br /> <i>The Storm Lord </i>Sacred Hunt grants your character the ability to clearly perceive prey that is possessed, Urged, or Claimed. If your character looks at a Ridden human who is the prey of the hunt, for example, she will see the spirit coiled up within him.<br /> <b>Source; </b>The Sacred Hunt rite, or being personally blessed by a Firstborn.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> The prey is brought down (a kill is not necessary) or the pack breaks off the Siskur-Dah by taking any significant actions towards ends other than the hunt.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Your character achieves an exceptional success on an action involving the prey.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>The Storm Lord and Bone Shadow's benefits are non-specific enough to include Ghosts and other stranger Ephemeral beings.<br /> <br /> I also like your plot point about the werebear curse, and think that if you want to keep werewolf ghosts extremely rare, make being the target of ghost forming powers be a prerequisite for becoming a Ghost if you're a werewolf would be a good step. To add depth to the story and be ready in case the players explore that lead, I'd have a rough idea about the rite the werebears used in case the PC investigate and want to learn it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-27-2017, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T01:54:18-08:00","id":1056023,"title":"","content":"You know, this thread is reminding me of the hypothetical werewolf-sineater cross template that's been talked about when the Admonitoria were revealed a while ago... Especially with the &quot;clawed his way out of the underworld&quot; wolf that Acrozatarim mentioned above. Wonder how that'd work out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T12:29:34-08:00","id":1056733,"title":"","content":"This is how I would run it, first I'd make the rite:<br /> <br /> <br /> Let's call the rite &quot;Restless Hibernation&quot;. The werebears did the rite against the Chieftain because of the horrible crimes he did against their people.<br /> <br /> My version would taking the werewolf to be turned into a ghost by ritually entombing them alive with any people or items that would be their Anchors if they were a human becoming a ghost. The werewolf will eventually suffocate, thirst or starve to death. If the werewolf is the first to be interned at the site, they leave behind a Geist but otherwise they leave a rank 2 ghost, with their Anchors being the items and remains of the persons buried with them.<br /> <br /> This is horribly macabre, and not something pulled off easily or lightly. I'd say a 4 dot rite. In this particular case the Werebears didn't seal the tomb to prevent air flow, and there was a drip of water within reach, ensuring a slower and more painful death of starvation. Also beside the Fetishes that the Chieftain owned, all the werewolves, wolf-blooded, and human members of his Pack were included in the burial. The wolf-blooded and humans left ghosts, which the Chieftain as a Geist devoured, with possible exception of whatever ghost I want to use as a plot clue, and that ghost escaped by using the Discorporate Manifestation and reforming at an Anchor that withstand the test of time so the PCs can find it, if that's how I would lead them to the burial site. I also have the Geist devour any spirits in Twilight at its burial site, such as the Hunger Spirits his and his compatriots' deaths would have caused. It isn't even needed for the PCs to be the one to release this being from its burial site, that could have happened decades or hundreds of year prior. It's Anchors could be spread across the world and it could use Discorporate to travel between them.<br /> <br /> In my example I'd have the Chieftain become a rank 3 Geist. I'd stat him like this:<br /> <br /> <b>Twilight Description to those that can see Ghosts:</b> This nine foot tall being looms in what appears to be an emaciated wolf-headed monster covered in matted fur, with hind legs like a bipedal wolf. Its bony hands are massive, and have wicked claws, eyes sunken and yet burn with rage, and its rib-cage a visible arch showing signs of extreme starvation. Werewolves would recognize it as a werewolf in Garu form that looks like its been starved past the point of madness.<br /> <br /> <b>Power:</b> 9<br /> <b>Finesse: </b>5<br /> <b>Resistance:</b> 9<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 20<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 9<br /> <b>Willpower: </b>10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 8<br /> <b>Corpus: </b>17<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Bane:</b> Werebears (After what they did to him, they become his greatest weakness)<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Must attempt to kill any Werebear he sees.<br /> <b>Influence: </b>Werewolves 3<br /> <b>Manifestations: </b>Claim, Discorporate, Possess, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Awe, Drain, Essence Thief-Spirits, Implant Mission, Pathfinder, Stalwart<br /> <br /> This Chieftain wasn't dumb, and neither is the geist he left behind, the corpses of his compatriots are long since dust and Claiming one of the fetishes risks destroying it. Without Image or Manifest, Implant Mission and Possessing are his only methods to contact werewolves without a ghost savvy intermediary. He could possess one of his Fetishes to carve messages, or use his Influence-Werewolves to add the Opened Anchor condition to allow him to Possess one of them. Keeping him an invisible, intangible presence that can Discorporate at will, possess the PCs,use Implant Mission to give visions to a pack's Cahalith, increases the mystery and horror if used correctly.<br /> <br /> Side note: This would be a great Geist for a Silent Threshold Sin-eater.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T09:27:30-08:00","id":1057124,"title":"","content":"I think Werewolves would have souls, I mean they're born human and at that point have a soul, so what happens to that soul when they become werewolves? <br /> <br /> And if they have a soul, then they should be able to produce a ghost. <br /> <br /> 1e and 2e Werewolf may have different answers to this question. <br /> <br /> Also Mages, if a Mage with Death 5 wants something that normally doesn't produce a ghost to produce a ghost, they can do that by creating a ghost for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T09:45:06-08:00","id":1057133,"title":"","content":"Werewolves are half human, half wolf spirits, <i>thinking</i> they are human before First Change. That's why I think that leaving Renown Spirit as their 'ghost'<br /> at death is more logical, in cosmological reasons. Also, I do not like that only 'ancestors' you can have is amalgamation of all previous members of your family line. Much better is to summon greategreatgreatdad 'Red Tooth that slayered Pure in his life crusade'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-02-2017, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T10:17:16-08:00","id":1057144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=1057124#post1057124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if they have a soul, then they should be able to produce a ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do have souls. Presence of souls have no-to-little bearing on ghosts. As noted, buildings, animals and towns have left ghosts, these things do not have souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T15:02:11-08:00","id":1057277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=1057133#post1057133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves are half human, half wolf spirits, <i>thinking</i> they are human before First Change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, then why do they have Integrity before the First Change instead of Harmony if no transforming act takes place? Wouldn't the change in the fundamental way they operate indicate that they were not in fact already werewolves, in the same sense caterpillars are not already butterflies?<br /> <br /> I don't think werewolves are any more werewolves before the change than a human is already a vampire before the embrace, and the mechanics support that view.<br /> <br /> Also since in 2nd edition you can become wolf blood by being exposed to Lunacy, the 1st edition ties of werewolf to genetic lineage is not as it was.<br /> <br /> This is off topic though. The topic is Ghost Werewolves, something that if a Ghost Town is possible isn't absurd, but rather likely something with a very particular constellation of prerequisites.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=1057144#post1057144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They do have souls. Presence of souls have no-to-little bearing on ghosts. As noted, buildings, animals and towns have left ghosts, these things do not have souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, towns and even trees can leave a ghost, as per <i>Ghost Stories</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 03-02-2017, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T19:58:16-08:00","id":1057414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=1057277#post1057277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, then why do they have Integrity before the First Change instead of Harmony if no transforming act takes place? Wouldn't the change in the fundamental way they operate indicate that they were not in fact already werewolves, in the same sense caterpillars are not already butterflies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's your answer. Caterpillars are the same animal as butterflies, but they don't actually look like butterflies at all. If you didn't know from the start that butterflies grow from caterpillars, you wouldn't know the two were the same animal, because of how dramatic the metamorphosis is, and you/d probably consider a caterpillar to be more like a grub or worm. The First Change is a metaphysical metamorphosis, as the Werewolf's spiritual side asserting itself. Untill they change, they have no &quot;Spirit&quot; side yet developed to lean toward, so at low Integrity/Harmony, they just lean toward &quot;nothing.&quot; Technically, they have Harmony, but since their Spirit side isn't grown in yet, decaying toward Spirit looks pretty much the same as a human decaying toward Zero Integrity. Since it looks pretty much the same, it makes more sense to represent it as the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T06:36:13-08:00","id":1057570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175983-werewolf-s-ghost?p=1057414#post1057414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, there's your answer. Caterpillars are the same animal as butterflies, but they don't actually look like butterflies at all. If you didn't know from the start that butterflies grow from caterpillars, you wouldn't know the two were the same animal, because of how dramatic the metamorphosis is, and you/d probably consider a caterpillar to be more like a grub or worm. The First Change is a metaphysical metamorphosis, as the Werewolf's spiritual side asserting itself. Untill they change, they have no &quot;Spirit&quot; side yet developed to lean toward, so at low Integrity/Harmony, they just lean toward &quot;nothing.&quot; Technically, they have Harmony, but since their Spirit side isn't grown in yet, decaying toward Spirit looks pretty much the same as a human decaying toward Zero Integrity. Since it looks pretty much the same, it makes more sense to represent it as the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solid and well thought out rebuttal. +1 Internet to you. I feel like this is off topic (Ghost Werewolves) but interesting enough to deserve its own thread.<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1057585-when-does-a-werewolf-count-as-a-werewolf\"> I'll be making one in a bit and then link from here.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 03-03-2017, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}